    {
      "id": "py301-md0",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "# Python 301 · Standard Library & Functional\n\nPython ships with a huge standard library — no install needed. This lesson tours the most useful modules and functional-style tools.\n\n**Prerequisites:** *Python 201*.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md1",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 1. datetime\n\nWork with dates, times, and durations.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-1",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\nnow = datetime(2026, 1, 15, 9, 30)\nprint(\"formatted:\", now.strftime(\"%A, %d %B %Y %H:%M\"))\n\ndeadline = now + timedelta(days=10, hours=6)\nprint(\"deadline: \", deadline)\nprint(\"remaining:\", deadline - now)",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md2",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 2. collections\n\n`Counter`, `defaultdict`, and `namedtuple` solve common problems elegantly.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-2",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "from collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\ntext = \"the quick brown fox the lazy dog the end\"\ncounts = Counter(text.split())\nprint(\"most common:\", counts.most_common(2))\n\ngroups = defaultdict(list)\nfor word in text.split():\n    groups[len(word)].append(word)\nfor length, words in sorted(groups.items()):\n    print(f\"{length}-letter: {words}\")",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md3",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 3. itertools\n\nLazy, composable iterator building blocks.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-3",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "from itertools import combinations, accumulate, groupby\n\nprint(\"pairs:\", list(combinations([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], 2)))\nprint(\"running sum:\", list(accumulate([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])))\n\ndata = [1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3]\nfor key, grp in groupby(data):\n    print(f\"{key}: {len(list(grp))}x\")",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md4",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 4. json & regular expressions\n\nParse/produce JSON with `json`; match patterns with `re`.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-4",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "import json, re\n\nrecord = {\"user\": \"ada\", \"scores\": [90, 85, 92]}\nblob = json.dumps(record)\nprint(\"json:\", blob)\nprint(\"parsed avg:\", sum(json.loads(blob)[\"scores\"]) / 3)\n\nlog = \"ERROR 2026-01-15 disk full; WARN 2026-01-16 low mem\"\nfor level, date in re.findall(r\"(ERROR|WARN) (\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2})\", log):\n    print(f\"{level:<5} on {date}\")",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md5",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 5. Functional tools\n\n`map`, `filter`, and generator expressions process data lazily and declaratively.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-5",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "from functools import reduce\n\nnums = range(1, 11)\nsquares = map(lambda n: n * n, nums)\nbig = filter(lambda n: n > 25, squares)\nprint(\"squares > 25:\", list(big))\n\nproduct = reduce(lambda a, b: a * b, range(1, 6))\nprint(\"5! =\", product)\n\n# Generator: lazy, memory-friendly\ndef fib():\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    while True:\n        yield a\n        a, b = b, a + b\n\ngen = fib()\nprint(\"first 10 fib:\", [next(gen) for _ in range(10)])",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md6",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "source": "## 6. Decorators\n\nA decorator wraps a function to add behavior — here, simple timing.",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-6",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "python",
      "source": "import time\nfrom functools import wraps\n\ndef timed(fn):\n    @wraps(fn)\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        start = time.perf_counter()\n        result = fn(*args, **kwargs)\n        ms = (time.perf_counter() - start) * 1000\n        print(f\"[{fn.__name__}] took {ms:.2f} ms\")\n        return result\n    return wrapper\n\n@timed\ndef sum_squares(n):\n    return sum(i * i for i in range(n))\n\nprint(\"result:\", sum_squares(100_000))",
      "output": "",
      "executionCount": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "py301-md7",
